  "case": "sequelize_exports",
  "why": "One shape per rule `settle` reads an imported model by (js-review-followup D5, D8), each model named differently from the binding that exports it, so no rule can hide behind a match on the model's name. A class exported under another name (`{ Performer: Soloist }`); every link of `exports.Stanza = exports.Couplet = define(\u2026)`; an ESM `export const` and `export { Noel as Carol }`; a whole-module import of a module whose default is one of its two models; a names-known map whose value this pass cannot name (`Object.assign(module.exports, { Rondo: m.rondo })`), which falls back to the model's name. Refused: a member of a member (`exports.api.Lyric`), a destructured `{ Aria }` of a module whose default *is* the model, a define written after `module.exports` was replaced, a top-level binding a hidden surface does not export, a case-aside match with two candidates, and a self-association only resolution reveals. `seed.js` holds a `define` whose `{ type: 'string' }` is an option, not a Sequelize type.",
